-- PREMIUM / HARD — Stimulus: Democracy
(gen_random_uuid(),'MULTIPLE_CHOICE',7,'READING','Comprehension – Literal',5,
'Democracy, derived from the Greek words meaning "rule of the people", is a system of government in which citizens have a say in how they are governed. Modern democracies typically operate as representative democracies, where citizens elect politicians to make decisions on their behalf. Australia''s democratic system is characterised by compulsory voting, a bicameral parliament and an independent judiciary. While democracy is widely regarded as the fairest system of government, it is not without its critics. Some argue that the complexity of modern governance requires specialised expertise that elected representatives may not possess. Others contend that compulsory voting undermines genuine political engagement by forcing participation from those who are uninformed or indifferent. Nonetheless, most political scientists agree that democracy, despite its imperfections, remains the most effective safeguard against abuse of power.','TEXT',
'PREMIUM','HARD',
'What is the literal meaning of the word "democracy"?','{"A":"Rule by experts","B":"Rule by the wealthy","C":"Rule of the people","D":"Rule by elected officials"}','{"value":"C"}','The passage states democracy is derived from Greek words meaning "rule of the people".','PUBLISHED',NOW(),NULL),
