'Which sentence is in the subjunctive mood?','{"A":"She studies every day.","B":"If she were to study, she would pass.","C":"She will study tomorrow.","D":"She has studied all week."}','{"value":"B"}','The subjunctive mood expresses hypothetical or contrary-to-fact conditions. "were" (not "was") signals the subjunctive.','PUBLISHED',NOW(),NULL),
