'Which option correctly identifies the type of sentence? "Although I enjoy swimming, I prefer to run."','{"A":"Simple sentence","B":"Compound sentence","C":"Complex sentence","D":"Compound-complex sentence"}','{"value":"C"}','A complex sentence has one independent clause ("I prefer to run") and one subordinate clause ("Although I enjoy swimming").','PUBLISHED',NOW(),NULL),
(gen_random_uuid(),'MULTIPLE_CHOICE',7,'GRAMMAR_PUNCTUATION','Punctuation',3,NULL,NULL,'ADVANCED','MEDIUM',
'Which sentence uses a colon correctly?','{"A":"The results were: surprising to everyone.","B":"The results surprised: everyone in the room.","C":"The results were clear: the team had won by a large margin.","D":"The team: had won by a large margin."}','{"value":"C"}','A colon follows a complete clause and introduces an explanation or elaboration.','PUBLISHED',NOW(),NULL),
(gen_random_uuid(),'MULTIPLE_CHOICE',7,'GRAMMAR_PUNCTUATION','Modifiers',3,NULL,NULL,'ADVANCED','MEDIUM',
'Choose the sentence with the correctly placed modifier.','{"A":"She only eats vegetables on Mondays.","B":"Only she eats vegetables on Mondays.","C":"She eats only vegetables on Mondays.","D":"She eats vegetables only on Mondays."}','{"value":"D"}','The modifier "only" should be placed immediately before the word it modifies. "only on Mondays" clarifies frequency, not the type of food or who eats.','PUBLISHED',NOW(),NULL),

