(gen_random_uuid(),'MULTIPLE_CHOICE',7,'GRAMMAR_PUNCTUATION','Rhetorical Devices',5,NULL,NULL,'PREMIUM','HARD',
'Which rhetorical device is used in the following: "Ask not what your country can do for you — ask what you can do for your country."','{"A":"Simile","B":"Anaphora","C":"Chiasmus","D":"Hyperbole"}','{"value":"C"}','Chiasmus reverses the grammatical structure in successive clauses: A-B / B-A.','PUBLISHED',NOW(),NULL),
(gen_random_uuid(),'MULTIPLE_CHOICE',7,'GRAMMAR_PUNCTUATION','Clauses',5,NULL,NULL,'PREMIUM','HARD',
'Which sentence contains both a relative clause and an adverbial clause?','{"A":"The book, which I read last week, is fascinating.","B":"The book that I read last week fascinated me because it had a twist ending.","C":"She read the book and enjoyed it.","D":"I read the book last week."}','{"value":"B"}','"that I read last week" is a relative clause; "because it had a twist ending" is an adverbial clause (cause).','PUBLISHED',NOW(),NULL),
(gen_random_uuid(),'MULTIPLE_CHOICE',7,'GRAMMAR_PUNCTUATION','Punctuation',5,NULL,NULL,'PREMIUM','HARD',
'Which is the correct use of a hyphen?','{"A":"The well known author spoke at the event.","B":"The well-known author spoke at the event.","C":"The author was well-known at the event.","D":"The author, well known, spoke at the event."}','{"value":"B"}','Hyphens connect compound modifiers when they come before a noun (well-known author), but not when they follow the noun.','PUBLISHED',NOW(),NULL),
(gen_random_uuid(),'MULTIPLE_CHOICE',7,'GRAMMAR_PUNCTUATION','Sentence Structure',5,NULL,NULL,'PREMIUM','HARD',
'Which option correctly identifies the sentence structure? "The scientist, who had spent years in the field, published her findings after the government, pressured by lobbyists, delayed the report."','{"A":"Simple sentence","B":"Compound sentence","C":"Complex sentence","D":"Compound-complex sentence"}','{"value":"D"}','The sentence contains two independent clauses joined by a relationship, each embedded with subordinate clauses — making it compound-complex.','PUBLISHED',NOW(),NULL),
(gen_random_uuid(),'MULTIPLE_CHOICE',7,'GRAMMAR_PUNCTUATION','Figurative Language',5,NULL,NULL,'PREMIUM','HARD',
'Which sentence uses synecdoche?','{"A":"The moon smiled down on the sleeping city.","B":"She gave a hand to help with the project.","C":"Life is a rollercoaster.","D":"He ran as fast as lightning."}','{"value":"B"}','Synecdoche uses a part to represent the whole: "a hand" represents the whole person helping.','PUBLISHED',NOW(),NULL),
(gen_random_uuid(),'MULTIPLE_CHOICE',7,'GRAMMAR_PUNCTUATION','Vocabulary',5,NULL,NULL,'PREMIUM','HARD',
'Which word best completes the sentence: "The politician''s ___ response deflected all criticism without addressing any of the substantive concerns."','{"A":"candid","B":"equivocal","C":"forthright","D":"resolute"}','{"value":"B"}','"Equivocal" means deliberately ambiguous or unclear, suitable for deflecting criticism without addressing concerns.','PUBLISHED',NOW(),NULL),
(gen_random_uuid(),'MULTIPLE_CHOICE',7,'GRAMMAR_PUNCTUATION','Clauses',5,NULL,NULL,'PREMIUM','HARD',
'In the sentence "It is essential that every student submit their work on time", the subordinate clause is an example of which clause type?','{"A":"Noun clause in subject position","B":"Adverbial clause of time","C":"Noun clause in object position","D":"Relative clause"}','{"value":"C"}','"that every student submit their work on time" is a noun clause functioning as the object of "It is essential".','PUBLISHED',NOW(),NULL),
